www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/lifestyle/food-and-drink/g39157589/spring-cocktails/" class="css-0 e1socmtw0">22 sunny cocktail recipes </a></nav><nav><a data-theme-key="base-link" href="//www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/beauty-hair/skincare/g70602309/best-peptide-serums/" data-vars-ga-ux-element="Top Touts" data-vars-ga-call-to-action="Peptide serums for glowy skin" data-vars-ga-outbound-link="//www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/beauty-hair/skincare/g70602309/best-peptide-serums/" class="css-0 e1socmtw0">Peptide serums for glowy skin</a></nav><nav><a data-theme-key="base-link" href="//www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/fashion/g70639323/best-wedding-reception-dresses/" data-vars-ga-ux-element="Top Touts" data-vars-ga-call-to-action="21 wedding after-party dresseses" data-vars-ga-outbound-link="//www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/fashion/g70639323/best-wedding-reception-dresses/" class="css-0 e1socmtw0">21 wedding after-party dresseses</a></nav><nav><a data-theme-key="base-link" href="//www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/beauty-hair/hair/a70673113/kicktail-bob-haircut-trend/" data-vars-ga-ux-element="Top Touts" data-vars-ga-call-to-action="Meet spring's most elegant cut" data-vars-ga-outbound-link="//www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/beauty-hair/hair/a70673113/kicktail-bob-haircut-trend/" class="css-0 e1socmtw0">Meet spring's most elegant cut</a></nav></nav></div></section><div style="width:0px;height:0px;pointer-events:none;opacity:0;" aria-hidden="true"></div><div id="gpt-leaderboard-ad" suppressHydrationWarning class="css-1uk3z28 ewg5wdb1"></div><header class="css-dxyhk8 e1f1sunr9"><section data-lazy-id="P0-8"><div class="css-z207vh ejvijei0"><div class="css-epvra4 e1f1sunr2"><nav aria-label="breadcrumbs" data-lazy-parent="P0-8" class="css-0 e3morl63"><ol itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/BreadcrumbList" data-theme-key="breadcrumbs-list" class="css-jp5pj0 e3morl62"><li itemprop="itemListElement" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/ListItem" class="css-zxq36b e3morl61"><a data-theme-key="base-link" itemprop="item" href="/uk/love-sex/" data-vars-ga-ux-element="Breadcrumbs" data-vars-ga-call-to-action="Love &amp; Sex" data-vars-ga-outbound-link="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/love-sex/" class="e3morl60 css-4mdlz3 e1socmtw0"><span itemprop="name">Love &amp; Sex</span></a><meta itemprop="position" content="1"/></li><li itemprop="itemListElement" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/ListItem" class="css-huh8md e3morl61"><a data-theme-key="base-link" itemprop="item" href="/uk/love-sex/a63686129/sigma-male/" data-vars-ga-ux-element="Breadcrumbs" data-vars-ga-call-to-action="Are ‘sigma males’ the key to understanding the manosphere to male loneliness pipeline?" data-vars-ga-outbound-link="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/love-sex/a63686129/sigma-male/" class="e3morl60 css-4mdlz3 e1socmtw0"><span itemprop="name">Are ‘sigma males’ the key to understanding the manosphere to male loneliness pipeline?</span></a><meta itemprop="position" content="2"/></li></ol></nav><h1 data-theme-key="content-header-title" class="css-1wcwu5d e1f1sunr8"><span aria-hidden="true" data-theme-key="title-design-element-before" class="css-0 e68yk9k0"></span>Are ‘sigma males’ the key to understanding the manosphere to male loneliness pipeline?<span aria-hidden="true" data-theme-key="title-design-element-after" class="css-0 e68yk9k1"></span></h1><div class="css-zn3ows e1f1sunr6"><p>Guys, idolising Patrick Bateman was always gonna cause some problems…</p></div><div class="css-1phtlbf e1f1sunr5"><address class="css-ucpgpa e1v8cotw2"><span data-theme-key="by-line-name" class="css-1vz6ivw e1v8cotw1">By <a data-theme-key="popover-trigger" title="Megan Wallace" alt href="/uk/author/232758/megan-wallace/" aria-expanded="false" aria-haspopup="dialog" class="er6ohko0 ekw8pnu1 css-1jabtmb e1socmtw0">Megan Wallace</a></span><time class="css-u1fe4v e1f1sunr4">Published: 06 February 2025</time></address></div><div data-theme-key="header-action-block" class="no-print css-wkpw2c e1f1sunr11"><div class="css-18jz25a e1f1sunr10"></div></div></div></div></section></header><div data-journey-hide="true" class="css-k008qs et2g3wt0"><div class="standard-container content-container article-container css-1q1kaac et2g3wt4"><div class="content-lead css-1f8o566 et2g3wt6"><div data-theme-key="lead-image-wrapper" data-journey-blur="true" class="content-lead-image css-sm2oir e17huqc62"><div class="css-96439d e17huqc61"><picture class="css-1oxikel e1i0vlu30"><source srcset="https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/f6ggka-67a4b1aa28d9f.jpg?crop=1.00xw:1.00xh;0,0" media="(min-width: 100rem)"/><source srcset="https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/f6ggka-67a4b1aa28d9f.jpg?crop=1.00xw:1.00xh;0,0&amp;resize=1800:*" media="(min-width: 90rem)"/><source srcset="https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/f6ggka-67a4b1aa28d9f.jpg?crop=1.00xw:1.00xh;0,0&amp;resize=1400:*" media="(min-width: 75rem)"/><source srcset="https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/f6ggka-67a4b1aa28d9f.jpg?crop=1.00xw:1.00xh;0,0&amp;resize=1200:*" media="(min-width: 73.75rem)"/><source srcset="https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/f6ggka-67a4b1aa28d9f.jpg?crop=1.00xw:1.00xh;0,0&amp;resize=1024:*" media="(min-width: 64rem)"/><source srcset="https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/f6ggka-67a4b1aa28d9f.jpg?crop=0.655xw:1.00xh;0.0612xw,0&amp;resize=980:*" media="(min-width: 48rem)"/><source srcset="https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/f6ggka-67a4b1aa28d9f.jpg?crop=0.655xw:1.00xh;0.0612xw,0&amp;resize=640:*" media="(max-width: 48rem)"/><img src="https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/f6ggka-67a4b1aa28d9f.jpg?crop=0.655xw:1.00xh;0.0612xw,0&amp;resize=640:*" alt="jan 21 2000 hollywood ca usa christian bale as patrick bateman in the thrilling horror drama american psycho directed by mary harron" title="Christian Bale as Patrick Bateman in American Psycho" width="4142" height="2700" decoding="async" fetchPriority="high" sizes="100vw"/></picture></div><figcaption data-theme-key="photo-credit-figcaption-lead-image" class="css-1wzj7tn e1g9hcy40"><span data-theme-key="photo-credit-creditor" class="css-1pzw7j5 e1geg53v2">Entertainment Pictures / Alamy Stock Photo</span></figcaption></div></div><div class="piano-ribbon"></div><div data-journey-body="standard-article" class="article-body-content article-body standard-body-content css-n3hm4j et2g3wt7"><section data-ad-exclude="true" data-lazy-id="P0-9"><div class="css-n530ec emt9r7s6"><h2 class="css-3xzbqy emt9r7s5">Jump to:</h2><ul class="css-l03nee emt9r7s4"><li class="css-1rrsnhj emt9r7s3"><a data-theme-key="base-link" href="#what-is-a-sigma-male" data-update-hash="true" data-dispatch-ga="{&quot;eventType&quot;:&quot;tableOfContents&quot;,&quot;eventName&quot;:&quot;&quot;}" class="emt9r7s2 css-buympw e1socmtw0">What is a ‘sigma male’?</a></li><li class="css-1rrsnhj emt9r7s3"><a data-theme-key="base-link" href="#what-is-the-sigma-grindset" data-update-hash="true" data-dispatch-ga="{&quot;eventType&quot;:&quot;tableOfContents&quot;,&quot;eventName&quot;:&quot;&quot;}" class="emt9r7s2 css-buympw e1socmtw0">What is the ‘sigma grindset’?</a></li><li class="css-1rrsnhj emt9r7s3"><a data-theme-key="base-link" href="#where-did-the-sigma-male-come-from" data-update-hash="true" data-dispatch-ga="{&quot;eventType&quot;:&quot;tableOfContents&quot;,&quot;eventName&quot;:&quot;&quot;}" class="emt9r7s2 css-buympw e1socmtw0">Where did the ‘sigma male’ come from?</a></li><li class="css-1rrsnhj emt9r7s3"><a data-theme-key="base-link" href="#should-we-be-worried-about-it" data-update-hash="true" data-dispatch-ga="{&quot;eventType&quot;:&quot;tableOfContents&quot;,&quot;eventName&quot;:&quot;&quot;}" class="emt9r7s2 css-buympw e1socmtw0">Should we be worried about it?</a></li></ul></div></section><div data-lazy-id="P0-10" data-node-id="1" class="body_content_break_0"></div><div data-piano-position="0" data-node-id="2"></div><div data-node-id="3" class="piano_inline_content_0"></div><p data-journey-content="true" data-node-id="4" class="css-6wxqfj emevuu60">What do Patrick Bateman, John Wick, Thomas Shelby from<em data-node-id="4.1"> <a href="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/entertainment/a39512845/peaky-blinders-film-release-date-cast/" target="_blank" data-vars-ga-outbound-link="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/entertainment/a39512845/peaky-blinders-film-release-date-cast/" data-vars-ga-ux-element="Hyperlink" data-vars-ga-call-to-action="Peaky Blinders" data-node-id="4.1.1" class="body-link css-ohbdae emevuu60">Peaky Blinders</a></em>, and Tyler Durden from<em data-node-id="4.3"> Fight Club </em>have in common? Besides the obvious (they’re all white, straight men) these characters are embodiments of the ‘sigma male’, a term you’ve probably seen online or maybe even heard uttered by some of the more ~problematic~ guys in your wider circle. But what exactly is a sigma male? And should we be worried? </p><div id="piano-paywall-container" data-node-id="5" class="piano-container"></div><div data-lazy-id="P0-11" data-node-id="6" class="body_content_break_1"></div><div data-piano-position="1" data-node-id="7"></div><div data-node-id="8" class="piano_inline_content_1"></div><p data-journey-content="true" data-node-id="9" class="css-6wxqfj emevuu60">For starters, a sigma male is a term that was popularised in the manosphere — AKA the toxic masculinity corner of the internet that made <a href="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/reports/a42913789/andrew-tate-online-misogyny/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" data-vars-ga-outbound-link="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/reports/a42913789/andrew-tate-online-misogyny/" data-vars-ga-ux-element="Hyperlink" data-vars-ga-call-to-action="Andrew Tate" data-node-id="9.1" class="body-link css-ohbdae emevuu60">Andrew Tate</a> famous — and is gaining traction on TikTok (there are a whopping five million videos under the #sigma hashtag).</p><div data-lazy-id="P0-12" data-node-id="10" class="body_content_break_2"></div><div data-piano-position="2" data-node-id="11"></div><div data-node-id="12" class="piano_inline_content_2"></div><p data-journey-content="true" data-node-id="13" class="css-6wxqfj emevuu60">The sigma male provides an alternative to the alpha male and beta male dichotomy, which stratifies men into dominants and subordinates. Sigmas are lone wolves who sit outside of social norms, gaining success through a steadfast dedication to the grind. Self-identifying as — or aspiring to be — a sigma male can be seductive to guys who don’t fit the alpha male mould, but it can be a dangerous path to <a href="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/love-sex/relationships/a62802709/male-friendship/" target="_blank" data-vars-ga-outbound-link="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/love-sex/relationships/a62802709/male-friendship/" data-vars-ga-ux-element="Hyperlink" data-vars-ga-call-to-action="loneliness and isolation" data-node-id="13.1" class="body-link css-ohbdae emevuu60">loneliness and isolation</a>. </p><section data-embed="watch-next" data-lazy-id="P0-13" data-node-id="14" class="embed"></section><div data-lazy-id="P0-14" data-node-id="15" class="body_content_break_3"></div><div data-piano-position="3" data-node-id="16"></div><div data-node-id="17" class="piano_inline_content_3"></div><p data-journey-content="true" data-node-id="18" class="css-6wxqfj emevuu60">To learn more about how we define sigma males, as well as some of the potential dangers of the archetype bleeding from URL to IRL, we tapped <a href="https://www.port.ac.uk/about-us/structure-and-governance/our-people/our-staff/lisa-sugiura" target="_blank" data-vars-ga-outbound-link="https://www.port.ac.uk/about-us/structure-and-governance/our-people/our-staff/lisa-sugiura" data-vars-ga-ux-element="Hyperlink" data-vars-ga-call-to-action="Lisa Sugiura" data-node-id="18.1" class="body-link css-ohbdae emevuu60">Lisa Sugiura</a>, associate professor in cybercrime and gender at the University of Portsmouth, to answer our need-to-know questions. </p><div data-embed="piano-activation-unit-inline-newsletter" class="piano-activation-unit-inline-newsletter css-18ziudv e1c8uadx0"></div><section data-node-id="20" data-lazy-id="P0-15"><h2 title="What is a ‘sigma male’?" data-anchor-id="what-is-a-sigma-male" class="body-h2 css-yth5d6 emt9r7s1"><strong data-node-id="20.0">What is a ‘sigma male’?</strong></h2></section><div data-lazy-id="P0-16" data-node-id="21" class="body_content_break_4"></div><div data-piano-position="4" data-node-id="22"></div><div data-node-id="23" class="piano_inline_content_4"></div><p data-journey-content="true" data-node-id="24" class="css-6wxqfj emevuu60">Given that sigma males are hypervisible on social media — TikTok videos with ‘X signs you’re a sigma male’ abound — you’ve probably heard the term before, but what exactly does it mean? Given the archetype’s association with solitude, you might not have met a sigma male in your day-to-day, so here’s what the expert had to say.</p><div data-lazy-id="P0-17" data-node-id="25" class="body_content_break_5"></div><div data-piano-position="5" data-node-id="26"></div><div data-node-id="27" class="piano_inline_content_5"></div><p data-journey-content="true" data-node-id="28" class="css-6wxqfj emevuu60">“A sigma male is someone who doesn’t conform to societal expectations or norms and operates largely outside of traditional hierarchies,” explains Sugiura. “They’re portrayed as loners or introverts who are comfortable with solitude, and they don’t need validation from others to feel secure or successful.”</p><section aria-labelledby="recirc-heading" data-lazy-id="P0-18" data-node-id="29" class="inline-content-module"><div class="css-1xa411s e1fx7w0v14"><header class="css-7oigtt e1fx7w0v11"><h2 id="recirc-heading" class="css-tumddm e1fx7w0v10">Everyone's clicking on...</h2></header><div class="feature-version-1 css-edr09c e1fx7w0v13"><div class="css-79elbk e1fx7w0v12"><div aria-hidden="true" class="cx-flex-module"><div class="cx-item"><div class="cx-item-image"></div><div class="cx-title-container"><div class="cx-item-title"></div></div></div><div class="cx-item"><div class="cx-item-image"></div><div class="cx-title-container"><div class="cx-item-title"></div></div></div><div class="cx-item"><div class="cx-item-image"></div><div class="cx-title-container"><div class="cx-item-title"></div></div></div></div><div id="piano-inline-content-module" class="piano-inline-content-module"></div></div></div></div></section><section data-embed="editorial-link" data-lazy-id="P0-19" data-node-id="30" class="embed"><aside class="css-xmoip0 e94w1mj12"><h6 class="css-pc3nh9 e94w1mj10"><span aria-hidden="true" data-theme-key="title-design-element-before" class="css-0 e68yk9k0"></span><span class="css-8lle59 e94w1mj8">Related Story</span><span aria-hidden="true" data-theme-key="title-design-element-after" class="css-0 e68yk9k1"></span></h6><ul class="css-c4s2gi e94w1mj11"><li class="css-1imzvpg e94w1mj9"><a data-theme-key="base-link" href="/uk/reports/a42913789/andrew-tate-online-misogyny/" data-vars-ga-call-to-action="The rise of the mega misogynists" data-vars-ga-ux-element="Editorial Links" data-vars-ga-outbound-link="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/reports/a42913789/andrew-tate-online-misogyny/" class="css-1jv459k e1socmtw0"><span aria-hidden="true" data-theme-key="title-design-element-before" class="css-0 e68yk9k0"></span><img src="https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/lead-min-1676477004.jpg?crop=1.00xw:0.385xh;0,0.267xh&amp;resize=300:*" alt title="The rise of the mega misogynists" width="120" height="100%" decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="css-1l0uuk1 e94w1mj6"/><div class="css-1ib98um e94w1mj7"><span class="css-8lle59 e94w1mj8">The rise of the mega misogynists</span></div><span aria-hidden="true" data-theme-key="title-design-element-after" class="css-0 e68yk9k1"></span></a></li></ul></aside></section><section data-node-id="31" data-lazy-id="P0-20"><h2 title="What is the ‘sigma grindset’?" data-anchor-id="what-is-the-sigma-grindset" class="body-h2 css-yth5d6 emt9r7s1"><strong data-node-id="31.0">What is the ‘sigma grindset’?</strong></h2></section><div data-lazy-id="P0-21" data-node-id="32" class="body_content_break_6"></div><div data-piano-position="6" data-node-id="33"></div><div data-node-id="34" class="piano_inline_content_6"></div><p data-journey-content="true" data-node-id="35" class="css-6wxqfj emevuu60">Whether or not you’ve got much of a clue about sigmas, you may well have seen memes and videos about the ‘sigma grindset’ pop up across your social feeds. A combination of the words ‘grind’ (to <a href="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/work/careers/a28698934/side-hustling-lack-of-sleep-burn-out-exhaustion/" target="_blank" data-vars-ga-outbound-link="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/work/careers/a28698934/side-hustling-lack-of-sleep-burn-out-exhaustion/" data-vars-ga-ux-element="Hyperlink" data-vars-ga-call-to-action="hustle" data-node-id="35.1" class="body-link css-ohbdae emevuu60">hustle</a>) and ‘mindset’ (you know that one), the word ‘grindset’ is used to describe sigmas’ determined, dogged work ethic.</p><div data-lazy-id="P0-22" data-node-id="36" class="body_content_break_7"></div><div data-piano-position="7" data-node-id="37"></div><div data-node-id="38" class="piano_inline_content_7"></div><p data-journey-content="true" data-node-id="39" class="css-6wxqfj emevuu60">“The term is used to describe a lifestyle, which is centred around relentless self-improvement, hard work, and independence,” Sugiura explains. “It’s an extreme associated with sigma males, who are often in isolation and avoid ‘distractions’ like social norms, expectations, relationships, or the opinions of others.”</p><section data-embed="pullquote" data-lazy-id="P0-23" data-node-id="40" class="embed"><blockquote data-theme-key="pullquote" class="css-1p3hlt2 e1f76l351"><span aria-hidden="true" data-theme-key="title-design-element-before" class="css-j0s2z1 e68yk9k0"></span><blockquote class="css-v6ldbv e1f76l350">“Sigma males avoid ‘distractions’ like social norms, relationships, or opinions of others”</blockquote><span aria-hidden="true" data-theme-key="title-design-element-after" class="css-14dtqm4 e68yk9k1"></span></blockquote></section><div data-lazy-id="P0-24" data-node-id="41" class="body_content_break_8"></div><div data-piano-position="8" data-node-id="42"></div><div data-node-id="43" class="piano_inline_content_8"></div><p data-journey-content="true" data-node-id="44" class="css-6wxqfj emevuu60">The term engages with online hustle culture, wherein working long hours and prioritising success are glamourised, often at the cost of work/life balance. When we see it pop up in social media, Sugiura adds, it’s often in the form of ‘motivational’ phrases like ‘don’t talk to me until I’m rich’ or in semi-ironic memes that play to the hyperbolic nature of sigma male culture. </p><div data-lazy-id="P0-25" data-node-id="45" class="body_content_break_9"></div><div data-piano-position="9" data-node-id="46"></div><div data-node-id="47" class="piano_inline_content_9"></div><p data-journey-content="true" data-node-id="48" class="css-6wxqfj emevuu60">For Sugiura, the uses of sigma grindset content, and the phrase more generally, can vary. “You see people referring to the ‘sigma grindset’ as a tongue-in-cheek way of framing intense work habits, while there are others that are really trying to adopt that mindset in search of personal growth.”</p><section data-node-id="49" data-lazy-id="P0-26"><h2 title="Where did the ‘sigma male’ come from?" data-anchor-id="where-did-the-sigma-male-come-from" class="body-h2 css-yth5d6 emt9r7s1"><strong data-node-id="49.0">Where did the ‘sigma male’ come from?</strong></h2></section><div data-lazy-id="P0-27" data-node-id="50" class="body_content_break_10"></div><div data-piano-position="10" data-node-id="51"></div><div data-node-id="52" class="piano_inline_content_10"></div><p data-journey-content="true" data-node-id="53" class="css-6wxqfj emevuu60">In 2010, the ‘sigma male’ term was coined by the far-right writer Theodore Robert Beale as a counterpoint to the alpha/beta male hierarchy. Later, from the 2010s, it gained wider recognition on sites like Reddit and 4Chan and was pushed into the mainstream via the Trojan horse of ironic memes that exaggerated supposed sigma male traits. </p><div data-lazy-id="P0-28" data-node-id="54" class="body_content_break_11"></div><div data-piano-position="11" data-node-id="55"></div><div data-node-id="56" class="piano_inline_content_11"></div><p data-journey-content="true" data-node-id="57" class="css-6wxqfj emevuu60">While the sigma male lifestyle was made famous by social media, its roots are elsewhere. Specifically, the phrase is inextricable from a wider framework of classifying and stratifying male personalities as alpha or beta, a concept which originates from observing animal behaviour. </p><div data-lazy-id="P0-29" data-node-id="58" class="body_content_break_12"></div><div data-piano-position="12" data-node-id="59"></div><div data-node-id="60" class="piano_inline_content_12"></div><p data-journey-content="true" data-node-id="61" class="css-6wxqfj emevuu60">“In the 1940s, the researcher Rudolf Shankle observed that in a wolf pack, there appeared to be a social hierarchy: one dominant alpha wolf that leads the pack and then other beta wolves who assume subordinate roles,” Sugiura explains. “Over time, these labels have been adapted and expanded to describe human social dynamics, particularly within the context of <a href="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/work/careers/a63421211/meta-ends-diversity-inclusion/" target="_blank" data-vars-ga-outbound-link="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/work/careers/a63421211/meta-ends-diversity-inclusion/" data-vars-ga-ux-element="Hyperlink" data-vars-ga-call-to-action="masculinity" data-node-id="61.1" class="body-link css-ohbdae emevuu60">masculinity</a> and relationships, and, more recently, in spaces like the so-called manosphere online.”</p><section data-embed="editorial-link" data-lazy-id="P0-30" data-node-id="62" class="embed"><aside class="css-xmoip0 e94w1mj12"><h6 class="css-pc3nh9 e94w1mj10"><span aria-hidden="true" data-theme-key="title-design-element-before" class="css-0 e68yk9k0"></span><span class="css-8lle59 e94w1mj8">Related Story</span><span aria-hidden="true" data-theme-key="title-design-element-after" class="css-0 e68yk9k1"></span></h6><ul class="css-c4s2gi e94w1mj11"><li class="css-1imzvpg e94w1mj9"><a data-theme-key="base-link" href="/uk/love-sex/relationships/a62802709/male-friendship/" data-vars-ga-call-to-action="The great gender friendship gap" data-vars-ga-ux-element="Editorial Links" data-vars-ga-outbound-link="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/love-sex/relationships/a62802709/male-friendship/" class="css-1jv459k e1socmtw0"><span aria-hidden="true" data-theme-key="title-design-element-before" class="css-0 e68yk9k0"></span><img src="https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/cs-mmh-header-6728e39c62480.jpg?crop=1xw:0.8890469416785206xh;center,top&amp;resize=300:*" alt title="The great gender friendship gap" width="120" height="100%" decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="css-1l0uuk1 e94w1mj6"/><div class="css-1ib98um e94w1mj7"><span class="css-8lle59 e94w1mj8">The great gender friendship gap</span></div><span aria-hidden="true" data-theme-key="title-design-element-after" class="css-0 e68yk9k1"></span></a></li></ul></aside></section><section data-node-id="63" data-lazy-id="P0-31"><h2 title="Should we be worried about it?" data-anchor-id="should-we-be-worried-about-it" class="body-h2 css-yth5d6 emt9r7s1"><strong data-node-id="63.0">Should we be worried about it?</strong></h2></section><div data-lazy-id="P0-32" data-node-id="64" class="body_content_break_13"></div><div data-piano-position="13" data-node-id="65"></div><div data-node-id="66" class="piano_inline_content_13"></div><p data-journey-content="true" data-node-id="67" class="css-6wxqfj emevuu60">Men <a href="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/love-sex/relationships/a60428017/tiktok-boy-sober-dating-trend/" target="_blank" data-vars-ga-outbound-link="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/love-sex/relationships/a60428017/tiktok-boy-sober-dating-trend/" data-vars-ga-ux-element="Hyperlink" data-vars-ga-call-to-action="swearing off all relationships" data-node-id="67.1" class="body-link css-ohbdae emevuu60">swearing off all relationships</a> and social ties and worshipping Patrick Bateman? Well, you can see where things might start to go wrong… </p><div data-lazy-id="P0-33" data-node-id="68" class="body_content_break_14"></div><div data-piano-position="14" data-node-id="69"></div><div data-node-id="70" class="piano_inline_content_14"></div><p data-journey-content="true" data-node-id="71" class="css-6wxqfj emevuu60">While discourse around sigma males is predominantly limited to the digital sphere, it can be hard to ignore the ways in which online culture has impacted the IRL world in recent years. So, amidst the <a href="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/reports/a46885783/rise-in-sexism-in-schools/" target="_blank" data-vars-ga-outbound-link="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/reports/a46885783/rise-in-sexism-in-schools/" data-vars-ga-ux-element="Hyperlink" data-vars-ga-call-to-action="rise of anti-feminism" data-node-id="71.1" class="body-link css-ohbdae emevuu60">rise of anti-feminism</a>, the unabated presence of misogyny, and the continued issue of <a href="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/reports/a37315945/incel-forums-what-happens/" target="_blank" data-vars-ga-outbound-link="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/reports/a37315945/incel-forums-what-happens/" data-vars-ga-ux-element="Hyperlink" data-vars-ga-call-to-action="incels" data-node-id="71.3" class="body-link css-ohbdae emevuu60">incels</a> who harbour bitter, anti-women sentiments, should we be concerned about the rise of the sigma male?</p><div data-lazy-id="P0-34" data-node-id="72" class="body_content_break_15"></div><div data-piano-position="15" data-node-id="73"></div><div data-node-id="74" class="piano_inline_content_15"></div><p data-journey-content="true" data-node-id="75" class="css-6wxqfj emevuu60">“Yes,” says Sugiura. “But, to preface my ‘yes’, I don’t mean that having goals or male self-improvement and aspirations are, in themselves, problematic. It’s the broader context that we need to be wary about.”</p><section data-embed="editorial-link" data-lazy-id="P0-35" data-node-id="76" class="embed"><aside class="css-xmoip0 e94w1mj12"><h6 class="css-pc3nh9 e94w1mj10"><span aria-hidden="true" data-theme-key="title-design-element-before" class="css-0 e68yk9k0"></span><span class="css-8lle59 e94w1mj8">Related Story</span><span aria-hidden="true" data-theme-key="title-design-element-after" class="css-0 e68yk9k1"></span></h6><ul class="css-c4s2gi e94w1mj11"><li class="css-1imzvpg e94w1mj9"><a data-theme-key="base-link" href="/uk/reports/a37315945/incel-forums-what-happens/" data-vars-ga-call-to-action="What happens on incel forums?" data-vars-ga-ux-element="Editorial Links" data-vars-ga-outbound-link="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/reports/a37315945/incel-forums-what-happens/" class="css-1jv459k e1socmtw0"><span aria-hidden="true" data-theme-key="title-design-element-before" class="css-0 e68yk9k0"></span><img src="https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/lead-1629213464.png?crop=1xw:1xh;center,top&amp;resize=300:*" alt title="Incel forums: What happens on them?" width="120" height="100%" decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="css-1l0uuk1 e94w1mj6"/><div class="css-1ib98um e94w1mj7"><span class="css-8lle59 e94w1mj8">What happens on incel forums?</span></div><span aria-hidden="true" data-theme-key="title-design-element-after" class="css-0 e68yk9k1"></span></a></li></ul></aside></section><div data-lazy-id="P0-36" data-node-id="77" class="body_content_break_16"></div><div data-piano-position="16" data-node-id="78"></div><div data-node-id="79" class="piano_inline_content_16"></div><p data-journey-content="true" data-node-id="80" class="css-6wxqfj emevuu60">As she sees it, the sigma male focus on hyper-independence encourages isolation, something that can have a drastic impact on <a href="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/body/health/a36571180/male-mental-health-advice/" target="_blank" data-vars-ga-outbound-link="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/body/health/a36571180/male-mental-health-advice/" data-vars-ga-ux-element="Hyperlink" data-vars-ga-call-to-action="male mental health" data-node-id="80.1" class="body-link css-ohbdae emevuu60">male mental health</a>. When facing a crisis, after all, we can’t always grind our way out of it — sometimes we need friendly faces and support. “The scientific evidence shows that, as humans, social interaction is necessary,” continues Sugiura. “People die from <a href="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/body/mental-health/a39965571/loneliness-tips/" target="_blank" data-vars-ga-outbound-link="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/body/mental-health/a39965571/loneliness-tips/" data-vars-ga-ux-element="Hyperlink" data-vars-ga-call-to-action="loneliness" data-node-id="80.3" class="body-link css-ohbdae emevuu60">loneliness</a>.” </p><div data-lazy-id="P0-37" data-node-id="81" class="body_content_break_17"></div><div data-piano-position="17" data-node-id="82"></div><div data-node-id="83" class="piano_inline_content_17"></div><p data-journey-content="true" data-node-id="84" class="css-6wxqfj emevuu60">In addition to the ways that it exacerbates the <a href="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/love-sex/relationships/a45157745/as-a-man-making-new-friends-can-be-tough-i-used-a-dating-app-to-find-some/" target="_blank" data-vars-ga-outbound-link="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/love-sex/relationships/a45157745/as-a-man-making-new-friends-can-be-tough-i-used-a-dating-app-to-find-some/" data-vars-ga-ux-element="Hyperlink" data-vars-ga-call-to-action="male loneliness epidemic" data-node-id="84.1" class="body-link css-ohbdae emevuu60">male loneliness epidemic</a>, sigma male culture can be a gateway drug into <a href="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/reports/a62828180/donald-trump-election-feminist-response/" target="_blank" data-vars-ga-outbound-link="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/reports/a62828180/donald-trump-election-feminist-response/" data-vars-ga-ux-element="Hyperlink" data-vars-ga-call-to-action="misogyny" data-node-id="84.3" class="body-link css-ohbdae emevuu60">misogyny</a>. When the values of independence, ambition, and self-reliance inherent to sigma male ideology are twisted and manipulated by manosphere groups, the result can be a dangerous superiority complex. “Sigma male culture may come with an underlying resentment towards those who are seen as less enlightened, like beta males or, more often than not, women,” Sugiura explains. “This can fuel <a href="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/love-sex/relationships/a63248154/retroactive-jealousy-or-sexism/" target="_blank" data-vars-ga-outbound-link="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/love-sex/relationships/a63248154/retroactive-jealousy-or-sexism/" data-vars-ga-ux-element="Hyperlink" data-vars-ga-call-to-action="negative attitudes" data-node-id="84.5" class="body-link css-ohbdae emevuu60">negative attitudes</a> about <a href="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/love-sex/relationships/a60293524/stay-at-home-girlfriend-tik-tok-trend-breakups/" target="_blank" data-vars-ga-outbound-link="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/love-sex/relationships/a60293524/stay-at-home-girlfriend-tik-tok-trend-breakups/" data-vars-ga-ux-element="Hyperlink" data-vars-ga-call-to-action="women’s roles" data-node-id="84.7" class="body-link css-ohbdae emevuu60">women’s roles</a> or behaviour in dating and <a href="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/love-sex/relationships/a61852249/unsupportive-partners-stress-sex-drive/" target="_blank" data-vars-ga-outbound-link="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/love-sex/relationships/a61852249/unsupportive-partners-stress-sex-drive/" data-vars-ga-ux-element="Hyperlink" data-vars-ga-call-to-action="relationships" data-node-id="84.9" class="body-link css-ohbdae emevuu60">relationships</a>.”</p><div data-lazy-id="P0-38" data-node-id="85" class="body_content_break_18"></div><div data-piano-position="18" data-node-id="86"></div><div data-node-id="87" class="piano_inline_content_18"></div><p data-journey-content="true" data-node-id="88" class="css-6wxqfj emevuu60">She also explains that some interpretations of the sigma male have indirect links to other staples of manosphere culture: incels and Men Going Their Own Way (or MGTOW, for short). </p><section data-embed="pullquote" data-lazy-id="P0-39" data-node-id="89" class="embed"><blockquote data-theme-key="pullquote" class="css-1p3hlt2 e1f76l351"><span aria-hidden="true" data-theme-key="title-design-element-before" class="css-j0s2z1 e68yk9k0"></span><blockquote class="css-v6ldbv e1f76l350">“Sigma male culture can fuel negative attitudes about women’s roles in dating”</blockquote><span aria-hidden="true" data-theme-key="title-design-element-after" class="css-14dtqm4 e68yk9k1"></span></blockquote></section><div data-lazy-id="P0-40" data-node-id="90" class="body_content_break_19"></div><div data-piano-position="19" data-node-id="91"></div><div data-node-id="92" class="piano_inline_content_19"></div><p data-journey-content="true" data-node-id="93" class="css-6wxqfj emevuu60">It’s likely you’ve already heard of incels – AKA involuntary celibates – men who are hostile towards women and conventionally attractive men, due to their lack of relationship success. For this group, the sigma male mentality can be a healing balm. “Incels may adopt a warped version of the sigma male concept to rationalise their lack of success with women, rejecting societal norms and using their perceived isolation as an excuse for their inability to form <a href="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/love-sex/relationships/a18749955/healthy-relationship-signs/" target="_blank" data-vars-ga-outbound-link="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/love-sex/relationships/a18749955/healthy-relationship-signs/" data-vars-ga-ux-element="Hyperlink" data-vars-ga-call-to-action="healthy relationships" data-node-id="93.1" class="body-link css-ohbdae emevuu60">healthy relationships</a>,” adds Sugiura.</p><div data-lazy-id="P0-41" data-node-id="94" class="body_content_break_20"></div><div data-piano-position="20" data-node-id="95"></div><div data-node-id="96" class="piano_inline_content_20"></div><p data-journey-content="true" data-node-id="97" class="css-6wxqfj emevuu60">MGTOW, on the other hand, is essentially a male separatist movement which, more often than not, can veer into extremist misogyny. Its devotees tend to be men who believe that <a href="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/love-sex/relationships/a60855327/why-is-celibacy-so-hot-right-now/" target="_blank" data-vars-ga-outbound-link="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/love-sex/relationships/a60855327/why-is-celibacy-so-hot-right-now/" data-vars-ga-ux-element="Hyperlink" data-vars-ga-call-to-action="rejecting relationships" data-node-id="97.1" class="body-link css-ohbdae emevuu60">rejecting relationships</a> with women is the key to self-empowerment. “[Men who self-identify as] sigma males might be drawn to the MGTOW philosophy as a way to escape the beta male lifestyle while cutting ties with women entirely,” Sugiura explains.</p><div data-lazy-id="P0-42" data-node-id="98" class="body_content_break_21"></div><div data-piano-position="21" data-node-id="99"></div><div data-node-id="100" class="piano_inline_content_21"></div><p data-journey-content="true" data-node-id="101" class="css-6wxqfj emevuu60">“Some individuals adopt a toxic version of both the sigma male and MGTOW philosophies, creating a dangerous feedback loop where <a href="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/love-sex/relationships/a61802165/dating-doomscrolling/" target="_blank" data-vars-ga-outbound-link="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/love-sex/relationships/a61802165/dating-doomscrolling/" data-vars-ga-ux-element="Hyperlink" data-vars-ga-call-to-action="disillusionment with relationships" data-node-id="101.1" class="body-link css-ohbdae emevuu60">disillusionment with relationships</a> and society fuels even more isolation and resentment towards women as well.”</p><div data-lazy-id="P0-43" data-node-id="102" class="body_content_break_22"></div><div data-piano-position="22" data-node-id="103"></div><div data-node-id="104" class="piano_inline_content_22"></div><p data-journey-content="true" data-node-id="105" class="css-6wxqfj emevuu60">It’s worth keeping in mind that the above is a worst-case scenario. What’s crucial, though, is that we get men talking and relating to a diverse range of people — and genders — in our communities. After all, extremism thrives in an echo chamber.</p><div data-piano-position="23" data-node-id="106"></div><div data-lazy-id="P0-44" data-node-id="107" class="body_content_break_23"></div><section data-embed="editorial-link" data-lazy-id="P0-45" data-node-id="108" class="embed"><aside class="css-xmoip0 e94w1mj12"><h6 class="css-pc3nh9 e94w1mj10"><span aria-hidden="true" data-theme-key="title-design-element-before" class="css-0 e68yk9k0"></span><span class="css-8lle59 e94w1mj8">Related Stories</span><span aria-hidden="true" data-theme-key="title-design-element-after" class="css-0 e68yk9k1"></span></h6><ul class="css-c4s2gi e94w1mj11"><li class="css-1imzvpg e94w1mj9"><a data-theme-key="base-link" href="/uk/reports/a46885783/rise-in-sexism-in-schools/" data-vars-ga-call-to-action="School in the era of Andrew Tate" data-vars-ga-ux-element="Editorial Links" data-vars-ga-outbound-link="https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/reports/a46885783/rise-in-sexism-in-schools/" class="css-1jv459k e1socmtw0"><span aria-hidden="true" data-theme-key="title-design-element-before" class="css-0 e68yk9k0"></span><img src="https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/feminism-is-a-chore-to-us-what-it-s-like-going-to-and-working-in-a-school-in-the-era-of-andrew-tate-65d70a4949b38.jpg?crop=0.966xw:0.962xh;0.0144xw,0&amp;resize=30